    "reason": "[ev-989a451dfcd4] and the rest of its section ([ev-4a489b1e9ff3], [ev-d6a3846e479f]) only say the `forceSlash` option \"has been removed\". They don't say whether configurations that still set it are silently ignored, rejected or cause an error, and they don't say the key must be deleted. The CRD validator also found that spec.stripPrefix.forceSlash is still in the v3.0.0 Middleware schema [ev-0842f8f3bd9d], so Kubernetes would not reject it at the schema level. Nothing in the evidence says whether Traefik still honours it, so choosing between setting-ignored, resource-rejected or a lesser kind would be a guess. To decide, I need upstream text or code showing what Traefik 3.0.0 does when a StripPrefix middleware sets forceSlash.",
